{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at that time.</b> When Sarah gave birth, the kings of the earth said: surely HaShem will fulfill His oath to Abraham, for He said, 'To your seed I have given this land, from the river of Egypt' etc. Therefore Abimelech asked him: 'if you will deal truly with me and with my son and with my grandson.' But Abimelech could not ask for more, for HaShem had said to Abraham, 'and the fourth generation shall return here' — that is, after the fourth generation of the Amorites, your children shall return and conquer this land. Therefore, when the second Abimelech came in the days of Isaac, he said, 'let a covenant be cut between us, between me and you,' and he did not ask him for his son and grandson, because it is written, 'and the fourth generation shall return here.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:12.314654015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}